  "published": "2026-06-24T19:13:49.92Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.1.11 (carries SpawnDev.SIPSorcery 10.0.7 answerer DTLS-role fix): when the desktop SipSorcery peer ANSWERS an offer it now honors the offerer's a=setup (RFC 4145 §4.1 / RFC 5763 §5) - an offer of setup:active is answered setup:passive (we become DTLS server) instead of unconditionally setup:active. Fixes a two-DTLS-clients collision (unexpected_message(10)) against offerers that request setup:active, e.g. the SpawnWear watch / libpeer. No change for the common browser setup:actpass offer path. v1.1.10 (rollup of 1.1.9-rc.1 numwant cap + 1.1.10 periodic re-announce): TrackerSignalingClient now re-announces periodically at the tracker-given interval. The announce-interval timer body was previously empty (announce-once on connect), so a thin initial swarm never grew; the JS bittorrent-tracker reference re-announces every interval to keep pairing newly-arrived peers. ReAnnounceAll re-sends a periodic announce (Event=null, FRESH offers per active room) at the tracker cadence; the Layers 1-3 offer/answer dedup guard against duplicate-PC SCTP cascade (regression-tested by TrackerSignaling_ReAnnounce_FiresAtTrackerInterval). Also: client-side numwant is now capped at 5 to match the JS reference (was 10). Full RTC PMT 324/0/3 GREEN. See SpawnDev.WebTorrent/Docs/protocol-reference/08-offer-pairing-and-dedup.md.",
